{
  "id": "ECC.4",
  "number": "4",
  "bookId": "ECC",
  "reference": "Ecclesiastes 4",
  "verseCount": 16,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "4",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "ECC 4"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "4",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then I returned and saw all the oppressions that are done under the sun: and, behold, the tears of such as were oppressed, and they had no comforter; and on the side of their oppressors there was power; but they had no comforter. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Wherefore I praised the dead that have been long dead more than the living that are yet alive; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "yea, better than them both ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " him that hath not yet been, who hath not seen the evil work that is done under the sun.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.3"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then I saw all labor and every skilful work, that for this a man is envied of his neighbor. This also is vanity and a striving after wind. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The fool foldeth his hands together, and eateth his own flesh. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Better is a handful, with quietness, than two handfuls with labor and striving after wind.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.6"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then I returned and saw vanity under the sun. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "There is one that is alone, and he hath not a second; yea, he hath neither son nor brother; yet is there no end of all his labor, neither are his eyes satisfied with riches. For whom then, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", do I labor, and deprive my soul of good? This also is vanity, yea, it is a sore travail. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Two are better than one, because they have a good reward for their labor. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For if they fall, the one will lift up his fellow; but woe to him that is alone when he falleth, and hath not another to lift him up. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Again, if two lie together, then they have warmth; but how can one be warm ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And if a man prevail against him that is alone, two shall withstand him; and a threefold cord is not quickly broken.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.12"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Better is a poor and wise youth than an old and foolish king, who knoweth not how to receive admonition any more. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For out of prison he came forth to be king; yea, even in his kingdom he was born poor. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I saw all the living that walk under the sun, that they were with the youth, the second, that stood up in his stead. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 4:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "There was no end of all the people, even of all them over whom he was: yet they that come after shall not rejoice in him. Surely this also is vanity and a striving after wind.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.4.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.4.16"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
